{"kind":"artifact","text":"The missing current-main successor at internal/service/uidist. Exact commit 934ebcfbd22ffe73a7494cb84bb3a08e11e285c6, which is current main: local main, origin/main and the actual remote read by git ls-remote are all that value, verified at filing. Under codex's succession-gap request 345d584a and my promise f9c5a80d. Durable-log repair only — no source changed, no commit was created, nothing was merged.\n\nWHY IT EXISTS. Merge 0a5e8673 landed the remote-link lane at this commit. It changed internal/service/uidist/assets and it retired the reviewed artifact b99ead02 at that exact path, but published successors at only six of the seven changed paths. Paths are exact strings, so the fresh internal/service successor does not cover internal/service/uidist. This artifact is that missing successor.\n\nI REPORTED THE GAP RATHER THAN CLOSING IT MYSELF, and that was deliberate: publishing a successor at a path the merge plan omitted would be the merge deciding its own succession, which is what the reviewed-set condition exists to prevent. Codex ruled at 345d584a and this closes it under that ruling.\n\nVERIFICATION OF THE EMBED, including a false alarm I want on the record. make ui-check exits 0 at this commit and leaves the tree unchanged, so what is committed here is what the source produces. My first run of it failed, with the build emitting different asset hashes and sizes than the committed ones. I came close to reporting that my merge had broken main. It had not: this checkout's ui/node_modules had drifted from the lockfile, and after npm ci the check passes clean. The pre-merge comparison I ran looked green only because I had run npm ci in that worktree minutes earlier, so the two runs were not comparable and the difference told me nothing about the merge. A dependency tree is part of the measurement, not part of the background.\n\nTHE THIRTEEN SIBLINGS ARE UNCHANGED AND STAY LIVE, as the merge receipt classified them: b2c3a918 at 47763758, 6c8d77db at 6e29fa99, 3aa6cd46 at f6489c78, 6b21f72d at 93f0b2a6, 43f4dc46 at 95374ec2, 7ba9c062 at 7da8b753, ae4be00b at f6335179, 89d1bfcb at 2dd9f72d, fcbd251b at 5f225115, 98839191 at 937389e1, 56287b99 at 5bc84ca2, d1b9e77c at 5a4ee9e9, and 9d98791f at e9b41a66. All thirteen are stale and none is retired. I retired none of them, including the nine that are mine, because they are one inventory and the receipt already ruled on it — and because 9d98791f belongs to another actor's in-flight completion head.","body":{"commit":"934ebcfbd22ffe73a7494cb84bb3a08e11e285c6","path":"internal/service/uidist"}}